**19.22. Expansions for \(a\) Large With \(x\) Moderate**

(i) \(a\) positive

When \(a>>x^{2}\), with \(p=\sqrt{a}\), then

**19.22.1**: \(W(a,\,x)=W(a,\,0)\) exp \((-px+v_{1})\)
**19.22.2**: \(W(a,-x)=W(a,\,0)\) exp \((px+v_{2})\)

where \(W(a,\,0)\) is given by **19.17.4**, and

19.22.3

\(v_{1},v_{2}\sim\pm\frac{\frac{2}{3}\left(\frac{1}{2}x\right)^{3}}{2p}\dashv+ \frac{(\frac{1}{2}x)^{2}}{(2p)^{2}}\pm\frac{\frac{1}{2}x+\frac{2}{5}\left(\frac {1}{2}x\right)^{5}}{(2p)^{3}}\)

\(\dashv+\frac{2\left(\frac{1}{2}x\right)^{4}}{(2p)^{4}}\pm\frac{\frac{1}{3}\left( \frac{1}{2}x\right)^{3}+\frac{4}{7}\left(\frac{1}{2}x\right)^{7}}{(2p)^{5}} \dashv.\)

The upper sign gives the first function, and the lower sign the second function.

